1zy4|n|Any one of numerous species of large aquatic birds belonging to Cygnus, Olor, and allied genera of the subfamily Cygninae. They have a large and strong beak and a long neck, and are noted for their graceful movements when swimming. Most of the northern species are white. In literature the swan was fabled to sing a melodious song, especially at the time of its death. ; Fig.: An appellation for a sweet singer, or a poet noted for grace and melody; as Shakespeare is called the swan of Avon. ; The constellation Cygnus.	a:1yel,64,5;28oj,51,2;1op7,48,2;7yj,48,4~1yel,64,5;7yj,48,4;28oj,51,2;1op7,48,2	n:dz4,97,5;7yj,28,1~dz4,97,5;7yj,28,1	N:bya,122,4;1c1w,96,2;1w3l,93,9;14z9,67,1;psw,56,3~1w3l,93,9;bya,122,4;psw,56,3;1c1w,96,2;14z9,67,1
