204e|n|A very large oceanic fish (Xiphias gladius), the only representative of the family Xiphiidae. It is highly valued as a food fish. The bones of the upper jaw are consolidated, and form a long, rigid, swordlike beak; the dorsal fin is high and without distinct spines; the ventral fins are absent. The adult is destitute of teeth. It becomes sixteen feet or more long. ; The gar pike. ; The cutlass fish. ; A southern constellation. See Dorado, 1.	n:99u,204,3~99u,204,3	N:29gb,193,5;1kcp,93,4~29gb,193,5;1kcp,93,4
